      "title": "Korean double vowels in one song! 와 워 위 의 #learnkorean",
      "text": "Sing and move along with Mongle — Korean double vowels in one song.\n\nTwo vowels glide into one:\n오 + 아 = 와 (wa) · 우 + 어 = 워 (wo) · 우 + 이 = 위 (wi) · 으 + 이 = 의 (ui)\nWith a consonant: 과 (gwa, as in 사과 apple) · 귀 (gwi, ear) · 쥐 (jwi, mouse) · 뭐 (mwo, what?)\nThe first vowel is coral, the second is blue — watch them join.\n\n\"오 더하기 아는?\" (o + a = ?) — say the answer before the song does!\nRomanization appears under every letter, and English captions (CC) have the lyrics.\nAt the end, try reading 봐 · 줘 · 쉬 before you hear them!\n\nHangul for Beginners · 한글 초보단계 #4 — after the vowel (#1), consonant (#2) and batchim (#3) songs.\nSYNK LAB · learn Korean the fun way, with Mongle.\n#learnkorean #hangul #koreanvowels",
      "alt": [
        "A felt kid and the coral felt mascot Mongle join two Korean vowels into one (오 + 아 = 와), first part coral and second part blue, under a white card reading “Korean double vowels in one song!”"
      ],
